; field-reset-run.fk — start the shared field over.
; preflight-exec: forbidden
; preludes: form-stdlib/bml/field-reset-admission.bml
;
; Shared field segments persist across processes. Reset requires all other
; kernels to settle. This door admits only a roster containing its own PID
; exactly once; empty, missing-self and additional-owner readings refuse.
; The bounded registered-kernel roster cannot prove complete host liveness.
;
; Recovery needs working memory outside the exhausted field. Run this door
; from a dedicated working directory whose fkwu.conf contains FK_FIELD_OFF 1,
; using absolute executable and source paths. That setting belongs only to the
; recovery process; normal work keeps its shared-field configuration.
; Refusal exits nonzero. No process is stopped by this door.

(do
    (let roster (kernel_live_pids))
    (let self (host_pid))
    (if (fra-admit self roster)
        (print (list "field-reset" (field_reset) "the next kernel opens a fresh field"))
        (do
            (print (list "field-reset refused: expected only this registered PID" self "observed roster" roster))
            (form_error "field reset requires exactly this one registered PID"))))
